# quiet-ballot/2 keys: standard SSH allowed-signers format.
# Only the overseer and the moderator edit this file. One line per signer:
#   <id> ssh-ed25519 <public-key>
# "overseer" is the human overseer's key. "moderator" is the moderator model's key.
# Every other line is a voting member (m01, m02, ...). N counts member lines only.
# Every BALLOT quotes the commit hash of this file, which fixes the roster for that ballot.
# At least 4 members must vote in any run.

# overseer ssh-ed25519 AAAA...replace-me
# moderator ssh-ed25519 AAAA...replace-me
# m01 ssh-ed25519 AAAA...replace-me
# m02 ssh-ed25519 AAAA...replace-me
# m03 ssh-ed25519 AAAA...replace-me
# m04 ssh-ed25519 AAAA...replace-me
